sub('**Compute that cannot see your data.** Deploy a WebAssembly app into a hardware-isolated VM of its own, check from your browser or the CLI which hardware and code it runs on, and pay per second by card or from a wallet.\n\nEnclave is source-available, commercial software ([license](#license)). This README separates what serves customers today from research and roadmap; the [threat model](#threat-model-what-you-are-trusting) below says what each kind of host protects you from and whom you still trust.', 'Enclave is a commercial, source-available compute platform under active development ([license](#license)). Deploy WebAssembly apps, inspect supported attestation evidence from a browser or CLI, and pay per second by card or from a wallet. **Protections depend on the host and verification path:** per-app separation does not by itself exclude the host OS or the operator. Windows host exclusion remains unproven in the documented evidence, and neither the platform nor Enclave Shield has had an external audit.\n\nThis README distinguishes documented deployments from research and the target architecture. The deployment snapshot below reflects repository evidence dated **2026-10-14 through 2026-10-18**, not a new check of current fleet health. Consult the [live fleet](https://enclave.host/develop#fleet) for availability and the [threat model](#threat-model-what-you-are-trusting) for protection limits. The [public claims policy](PRODUCT.md#public-claims-policy) requires these distinctions wherever capabilities are presented.')
